From: LightMoss <lightmoss@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: odroidgo3-joypad: no 1 s rumble at probe

The probe ran the rumble for a second with msleep(1000). The driver is
built in, so that second was spent inside the kernel's initcalls: the
root filesystem was mounted, and userspace started, a second later on
every boot (joypad_probe took 1.007 s on a G80CA). On the G80CA the
"rumble" is the blue LED, so all it did was blink it at boot.
---
--- a/drivers/input/joystick/odroidgo3-joypad.c
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/odroidgo3-joypad.c
@@ -2726,14 +2726,11 @@
 		return error;
 	}
 
-	/* 启动震动: 探测时振动1秒 */
-	if (joypad->has_rumble) {
-		joypad->level = 0xFFFF;
-		joypad_vibrator_start(joypad);
-		msleep(1000);
-		joypad_vibrator_stop(joypad);
-		joypad->level = 0;
-	}
+	/*
+	 * LightMoss: no 1 s rumble at probe. The driver is built in, so its
+	 * msleep(1000) held up the whole kernel boot (and the root mount) by
+	 * a second, to blink the LED that stands in for the G80CA's motor.
+	 */
 
 	dev_info(dev, "%s : probe success\n", __func__);
 	return 0;
